# Context Before Code

Before examining any code in this repo, **always** look for a `.context/` directory alongside it and read any `*-context.md` file there first.

## Why

Context files explain the *purpose*, *rationale*, and *design decisions* behind the code. Reading code without them means reverse-engineering intent that is already documented.

## How

1. When you open or are pointed at a directory (e.g. `primitives/actions/`), check for `.context/*-context.md` in that directory.
2. Read it fully before reading any source files.
3. Use it to orient every subsequent code read — treat it as the "why" lens for everything you see in the code.

## Example

```
primitives/actions/
  .context/
    module-context.md   ← read this FIRST
  __init__.py
  _runner.py
  ...
```

`module-context.md` explains purpose, public API, seam, dependencies, and known scan violations — all context the code itself cannot convey concisely.

## Rule

> No code read without a context-file check first. If no `.context/` exists, note the gap and proceed.
